`--pipeline-profile` now also records front-end events, each with the running thread's CPU time and allocated bytes: every file parsed or `.doo` file read, the module dependency graph, each module's resolution and its phases, each global resolution pass, and each module's translation to Boogie; and `dafny resolve` accepts it. Hidden options add the live heap after forced collections, the runtime's GC events, and hold points for heap dumps. Dafny's other output is unchanged (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/241).
